We need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta. To stage, we need loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, etc. Actually stage_schedule_candidate action: precondition includes candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading. So we need to have loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked for shift_candidate_beta. Currently shift_candidate_beta has candidate_loading_container_linked loading_container_beta (init). loading_container_beta is available (init). We need to load container onto leg: load_container_onto_leg action requires candidate_prepared, candidate_transport_leg_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_available, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded. So we need to assemble transport leg and authorize loading.

Transport leg: we have transport_leg_alpha available initially. We need to assemble it (assemble_transport_leg or one of the specialized assemble actions). For loading container to be linked, we need transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. Also need origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded depending.

We need to decide whether we will load cargo onto leg at origin or destination? The goal includes loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha and loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta. So we need to load container onto leg (makes loading_container_loaded and leg_linked). This action does not set origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded; those are set by assemble actions (origin_leg_loaded, destination_leg_loaded, etc). Actually loading_container_leg_linked is an effect of load_container_onto_leg (makes it linked). So we need to execute load_container_onto_leg for shift_candidate_beta? Wait load_container_onto_leg parameters: ?candidate - schedule_candidate ?loading_container - loading_container ?transport_leg - transport_leg. It does not require candidate_prepared? Actually its precondition includes candidate_prepared ?candidate. So we need shift_candidate_beta prepared before loading.

Thus steps for shift_candidate_beta: prepare, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, assign operator, assign skill certificate, load container onto leg (requires transport leg assembled and loading authorized), then stage_schedule_candidate (which also requires candidate_prepared, loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading). After staging, we need to establish clearance (some variant), then maybe set route sequence context, validate route sequence, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, etc.

